  "what_this_is": "A column-grounding benchmark for measuring what schema-name modes cost. Each question names a table and asks which of its columns answers it. The columns are the real columns of the three golden tables, with the role and logical type the semantic catalog (L0) assigns them. The scorer is a deterministic keyword matcher standing in for an LLM; 'knowledge' is the world knowledge it is allowed, applied to the question side only. Numbers from it measure RELATIVE capability loss between FULL, DESCRIBED and OPAQUE; they are not a claim about any particular model's accuracy.",
